    "evidence_text": " She was in several movies including \"Blue Hawaii\", \"The Singing Nun\" and \"Monster on the Campus\".\n\nThe Singing Nun\n\nJeanne-Paule Marie \"Jeannine\" Deckers (17 October 1933 \u2013 29 March 1985), better known as S\u0153ur Sourire (\"Sister Smile\", often credited as The Singing Nun in English-speaking countries), was a Belgian singer-songwriter and initially a member of the Dominican Order in Belgium as Sister Luc-Gabrielle.\n\nKatrina Conder\n\nKatrina Conder is an Australian television presenter.\n\n Katrina starred in a lead role in the 2005/06 9minds production of Black Rock\n\nThe Singing Nun (film)\n\nThe Singing Nun is a 1966 American semi-biographical film about the life of Jeanine Deckers, a nun who recorded the chart-topping hit song \"Dominique\".\n\n It starred Debbie Reynolds in the title role.\n\n The film also stars Ricardo Montalb\u00e1n, Katharine Ross, Chad Everett, and Ed Sullivan as himself.\n\n The film stars C\u00e9cile de France as Jeannine Deckers, also known as The Singing Nun).\n\nKatharine Ross",
